  "narrative": "No independent validation has been delivered and there are no validation response deadlines. Therefore, synthesis is limited to the discovery evidence already available. The current claim set contains no scientifically meaningful supported association with outcome_001. All tested contrasts had sufficient cell sizes and valid Welch tests. Because the estimates and intervals are signed to the registered negative/stronger-dependency direction, a meaningful positive claim requires evidence for a signed effect above +0.15 composite dependency-score units. None do. The described research markers show negligible overall effects: feature_007 is near zero and slightly opposite the claim (R1 signed estimate -0.019; 95% CI -0.077 to +0.039), feature_058 is essentially null (R2 +0.008; CI -0.050 to +0.065), and feature_015 is a small positive signed effect far below threshold (R3 +0.039; CI -0.019 to +0.096). The corresponding marker effects restricted to high research-signature groups are also not supported: feature_007 among high feature_038 (R4 -0.072; CI -0.198 to +0.054), feature_058 among high feature_018 (R6 -0.061; CI -0.180 to +0.059), and feature_015 among high feature_036 (R8 +0.006; CI -0.115 to +0.126). The high-signature marker interactions are likewise unsupported and below threshold: feature_007 with high feature_038 (R5 -0.066; CI -0.208 to +0.075), feature_058 with high feature_018 (R7 -0.089; CI -0.225 to +0.047), and feature_015 with high feature_036 (R9 -0.043; CI -0.180 to +0.094). Among the initial additional binary predictors, the nearest threshold-relevant signals are feature_031 (R10 signed estimate +0.061; CI -0.008 to +0.129) and feature_050 (R12 +0.029; CI -0.091 to +0.148), but neither exceeds the +0.15 threshold and both have intervals compatible with small or null effects. feature_041 is clearly small (R11 +0.018; CI -0.049 to +0.086). These are negative or nonthreshold findings in this supplied dataset, not evidence for causal or generalized biological effects. Independent validation was not requested because no candidate has enough discovery signal to justify it. The most informative next analysis is to run the already registered broad screen of common binary predictors H13-H24, which includes feature_010, feature_048, feature_037, feature_023, feature_002, feature_003, feature_001, feature_035, feature_063, feature_033, feature_060, and feature_043. If a new contrast produces a signed estimate above +0.15 with uncertainty excluding the threshold in the claimed direction, I would accept it and consider validation and subgroup/interaction refinements. If it produces a similarly opposite meaningful effect, I would propose a reversed claim. Near-threshold imprecise contrasts such as feature_031 and feature_050 remain deferred rather than active follow-up candidates unless later evidence strengthens them.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 1 synthesis: no validation returned. No accepted claims yet. Negative/nonthreshold discovery evidence: research markers feature_007, feature_058, feature_015 are not meaningful overall main effects on outcome_001. High-signature marker subsets (threshold >=0.75 SD for feature_038, feature_018, feature_036) and marker interactions are also not supported at threshold 0.15. Initial binary screens: feature_031 is closest in favorable direction but only +0.061 signed, upper CI 0.129, rejected/deferred; feature_050 is imprecise, upper CI 0.148, rejected/deferred; feature_041 negligible. Plan for next analyses: prioritize registered common binary predictors H13-H24: feature_010, 048, 037, 023, 002, 003, 001, 035, 063, 033, 060, 043. If any has signed estimate >0.15 and CI supporting threshold, accept, request validation if useful, and propose interaction/subgroup refinements. If near-threshold only, defer unless a follow-up contrast strengthens it. If strong opposite direction appears, create reversed claim rather than reinterpreting. All conclusions remain dataset-specific and observational; biological meaning of constructed features is unknown."
}
